Credential Manager attributes, and CloseThreadWaitChainSession.

From vstenv (https://github.com/dguedry/vstenv, patches/wine/advapi32-credential-attributes-11.17.patch),
by its authors, under Wine's licence (LGPL-2.1-or-later); it applies to Torquio's zhiyi/wine base unchanged.

Wine's CredWriteW didn't store a credential's Attributes and CredReadW returned none. Steinberg's License
Engine writes its refresh token as a generic credential with one attribute (its format marker); read back
without it, the engine logs "1.1 Format refresh token detecting -- resetting", deletes the token and signs the
user out, so the Activation Manager asked for a sign-in every time. Attributes are now stored as
"Attribute<n>" binary values and read back. The same patch exports CloseThreadWaitChainSession (a no-op; Wine's
OpenThreadWaitChainSession hands out NULL), which HALion Sonic calls on exit.

--- a/dlls/advapi32/cred.c
+++ b/dlls/advapi32/cred.c
@@ -77,6 +77,96 @@
